{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/66457-understanding-the-agendas","id":66457,"title":"Understanding the Agendas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-06T07:10:51-08:00","id":66457,"title":"Understanding the Agendas","content":"So... I've run into no few people who have problems understanding the Integrator agenda. Personally, I've always found them, and the Tempters, to be the easiest of the agendas to wrap my head around, and Interrogators the hardest. So, I had a thought. Lets here from everyone what they think their favorite Agendas really stand for.<br /> <br /> Integrators realize that the God Machine is necessary to the world. Without it, the Y2K bug would have shunted humans into a new dark age (at least according to Seattle!). Without it, an asteroid would be heading towards the Earth on a collision course. A world without the God Machine - Hell - would be one of suffering as no one would be there to shield humanity from actual huge disasters. And who knows what dark hungry thing would assume its place? At least the God Machine is the devil you know, and it could always be worse. And, so, because getting rid of God Machine isn't desirable, that leaves trying to fix the system. They approach the matter in different ways, but often with the end goal of &quot;bring change and a better method to the God Machine.&quot;<br /> <br /> Tempters, on the other hand, don't really think that rejoining, or directly fighting, the God Machine is worth it. No, every one Fell for a reason. Chances are, rejoining will just have you recycled. That's not worth it. And waging war? Well, if you fell for Love, or pleasure, or because you wanted to protect something? War has a nasty tendency of collateral damage, and those things you care about tend to end up as hostages, &quot;friendly fire&quot; targets, or just flat out targets of your enemies. Tempters Fell for this world, and they want to enjoy it. So, what's an Unchained to do? Why, build a &quot;criminal&quot; empire that won't be the target of the God Machine. Suborn Infrastructure and boltholes you can relax in, build up covers that reflect the kind of life you want to live. An ideal for a Tempter is to have a bubble universe where they can do what they want without repercussions from the law of the God Machine, yet still reap the benefits it provides everyone else - see Madam Damnation in Seattle. They're not like Sabatuers who want to destroy the God Machine - they just want it out of their lives, and they'll build and arrange things to make it so. Selfish, perhaps. But you don't Fall for selfless reasons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T08:46:42-08:00","id":66515,"title":"","content":"I was totally on board with the Reconcilers in Demon: the Fallen, but the Integrators threw me for a loop at first. The hardest thing for me to figure out was what possible incentive a demon could give the God-Machine to let it back in on its own terms. You might think God is actually helping humanity, good outweighs the bad, there's an ultimate benevolent design that isn't obvious, but what could you possibly offer to make it stop actively trying to kill you and, in some way, admit it was wrong to cast you out? I don't remember any quotes from the text that supported the idea that re-integrating on your own terms is a reasonable goal, had been done before, or was even possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T09:18:08-08:00","id":66531,"title":"","content":"You could say the same about all the Agendas: how can it be possible for the Saboteurs to destroy the God-Machine, or the Tempters to free themselves from the danger of it finding them, or the Inquisitors to figure it out? I suspect many Integrators might think this is a test - reacceptence while retaining free will is something that must be earned, and perhaps something that must be pursued as a matter of faith (both the shallow kind of having no proof that it's possible, and the deeper kind of trusting in the God-Machine's better nature) - which could be taken to imply that it's the most religious of the Agendas (as opposed to the mystical/gnostic Inquistitors, the quasi-atheistic Tempters, and antinomian Saboteurs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T20:28:10-08:00","id":66951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/66457-understanding-the-agendas?p=66515#post66515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was totally on board with the Reconcilers in Demon: the Fallen, but the Integrators threw me for a loop at first. The hardest thing for me to figure out was what possible incentive a demon could give the God-Machine to let it back in on its own terms. You might think God is actually helping humanity, good outweighs the bad, there's an ultimate benevolent design that isn't obvious, but what could you possibly offer to make it stop actively trying to kill you and, in some way, admit it was wrong to cast you out? I don't remember any quotes from the text that supported the idea that re-integrating on your own terms is a reasonable goal, had been done before, or was even possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that a) it is possible to literally change God's mind by hacking the right heavily-guarded locations and b) the largest faction of the Integrators has reintegration as their goal with the aim of changing the nature of the Machine by their absorption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T05:55:01-08:00","id":67130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/66457-understanding-the-agendas?p=66515#post66515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was totally on board with the Reconcilers in Demon: the Fallen, but the Integrators threw me for a loop at first. The hardest thing for me to figure out was what possible incentive a demon could give the God-Machine to let it back in on its own terms. You might think God is actually helping humanity, good outweighs the bad, there's an ultimate benevolent design that isn't obvious, but what could you possibly offer to make it stop actively trying to kill you and, in some way, admit it was wrong to cast you out? I don't remember any quotes from the text that supported the idea that re-integrating on your own terms is a reasonable goal, had been done before, or was even possible.</div> </div> </div> </div> Easy. The God Machine isn't some monolithic entity. Its more like the internet - a large web of computers that span the entire world and work together.<br /> <br /> So, to change the God Machine, they upload themselves as new aspects or new programming into the various &quot;servers&quot; of that giant web. And, yes, like Satchel says, no one said that the God Machine had to be -willing- to allow Integrators back in. Indeed, I think that most Integrators want to angle for the hacking-in angle - submitting not only means losing one's free will and memory, but they also have any elements that would result in making a better God Machine end up deleted.<br /> <br /> And, frankly, if all you wanted was to go back to the God Machine? Just go up to the nearest angel, submit yourself, and they'll take you in for reprogramming. That's not hard. No, Integrators want to get back on their terms, and given the spy themes, that means sneaking in.<br /> <br /> There's a reason that there's a side bar that talks about how the Demons have realistic goals when they're talking about hacking in, or building Hell, or killing the god Machine. Because its possible for all these to happen. Demons can reshape reality. The problem is just one of power - the God Machine has more.<br /> <br /> So, how about those Saboteurs or Interrogators? Anyone else with thoughts on Tempters?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - Also, I never said that anything about a benevolent ultimate design. Chances are, there's not - the God Machine has no concept of benevolence or malevolence. Its cold, unemotional, and detached. However, it IS tied to humanity, and will protect the greater good for its own reasons. The problem is that it has no problem committing horrors along the way, so long as the greater good, the status quo (ie Order) is maintained. Its kind of the ultimate tyrant. <br /> <br /> Sabateurs, for instance, see themselves as freedom from that tyrant and overthrowing him instead of effecting changes from the inside. Once the tyrannical God is gone, they can replace him with something better, and all those other pesky problems that come up will be dealt with when they come up. Because, if they can kill God, then they can probably stand up to whatever comes after him. Imagine being able to Go Loud to fight pretty much anything without fear of reprisal from angels. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-07-2014, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T07:50:59-08:00","id":67193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/66457-understanding-the-agendas?p=67130#post67130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how about those Saboteurs or Interrogators? Anyone else with thoughts on Tempters?</div> </div> </div> </div>It took me a while to parse together the general nature of the Inquisitors' &quot;enlightenment&quot;-based &quot;personal Hell,&quot; but it finally clicked for me a couple weeks ago:<br /> <br /> The Paranoids are after peace of mind. They want the God-Machine to not know they're there or be unable to harm them no matter where they go, through some change to their own nature or mindset. Their aims to this end might include excising the troublesome instincts left over from their Incarnation, or developing an alchemical substance that will strengthen their Primum so their unfettered <i>being</i> is a metaphysical constant, or reaching a techgnostic state of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wu_wei\" target=\"_blank\">wu wei</a> where their thoughts and actions don't register to the God-Machine. Whatever the method, the point is it's an alteration to the demon's own existence with the goal of turning their individual Fall into a completed Descent.<br /> <br /> The Saboteurs and the Tempters want to create Hell and the Integrators want to escape Hell, but the Inquisitors want to <i>be</i> Hell.<br /> <br /> It's kind of Miltonian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-07-2014, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}